  <section class="sec" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
    <span class="ghost" data-ghost="1" style="top:12%" aria-hidden="true">Geoscience</span>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="about-h" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)">About</h2>
      <p class="statement" id="statement">Researcher and engineer working where machine learning meets the earth sciences. I care about clean data pipelines, honest evaluation on imbalanced geological data, and models that people can call from a browser.</p>
      <div class="about-row">
        <div class="facts">
          <div class="fact"><b>Project Research Assistant</b><span>IIT Bombay, on the Dhatuveda project, since July 2025</span></div>
          <div class="fact"><b>Research Intern</b><span>Machine Intelligence Group (NCAIR), IIT Bombay, March to July 2025</span></div>
          <div class="fact"><b>B.E. Artificial Intelligence and Data Science</b><span>A.C. Patil College of Engineering, 2020 to 2024, CGPI 8.60</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="res-top">
        <h2 class="h2" id="research-h" data-reveal>Research</h2>
        <p class="lead" data-lines>Two years of applied work at IIT Bombay, from training models on geological tables to serving them to collaborators.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="field-pin" id="fieldPin">
      <figure class="field" id="fieldFig">
        <canvas id="field" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of a synthetic prospectivity map. Move the pointer over it to heat up cells."></canvas>
        <div class="field-over" id="fieldOver">
          <h3 data-reveal>Dhatuveda</h3>
          <p>Machine learning and deep learning on large-scale geoscience datasets, built to support mineral exploration.</p>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mono">Synthetic surface for illustration. Brighter cells stand for higher predicted prospectivity.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="tl-wrap">
        <span class="tl-line" id="tlLine" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <ol class="tl">
          <li>
            <div>
              <h3 data-reveal>Project Research Assistant</h3>
              <p class="org">Department of Mechanical Engineering, IIT Bombay</p>
              <span class="when mono">July 2025 to present</span>
            </div>
            <ul>
              <li data-lines>Working on the Dhatuveda project, applying machine learning and deep learning to large-scale geoscience datasets to support mineral exploration.</li>
              <li data-lines>Designed the full data pipeline: preprocessing and visualization with Pandas, Matplotlib and Plotly, then model building and training with Scikit-learn and PyTorch.</li>
              <li data-lines>Built FastAPI endpoints that serve predictive models and visualizations to research collaborators.</li>
              <li data-lines>Work closely with senior researchers to meet project deadlines, and mentor interns.</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div>
              <h3 data-reveal>Research Intern</h3>
              <p class="org">Machine Intelligence Group (NCAIR), IIT Bombay</p>
              <span class="when mono">March to July 2025</span>
            </div>
            <ul>
              <li data-lines>Built and trained models with scikit-learn and PyTorch to predict geological outputs.</li>
              <li data-lines>Applied statistical techniques to handle imbalanced data in geological datasets.</li>
              <li data-lines>Represented categorical features with vectorization so models could take them as input.</li>
              <li data-lines>Analyzed model performance and refined the data representation for better accuracy.</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div>
              <h3 data-reveal>B.E. Artificial Intelligence and Data Science</h3>
              <p class="org">A.C. Patil College of Engineering</p>
              <span class="when mono">2020 to 2024</span>
            </div>
            <ul>
              <li data-lines>Graduated with a CGPI of 8.60.</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="pj-head">
        <h2 class="h2" id="projects-h" data-reveal>Selected projects</h2>
        <p class="lead" data-lines>Three side projects in computer vision and generative media. Move your pointer over the artwork to play with it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pj-list" id="pjList">

        <article class="pj" style="--i:0">
          <div class="pj-in">
            <div class="pj-viz">
              <canvas class="pj-art" data-art="flow" role="img" aria-label="Animated flow field of coral and cyan particles"></canvas>
            </div>
            <div class="pj-info">
              <span class="pj-kind">Computer vision</span>
              <h3 class="pj-title" data-reveal>Reality Gaming</h3>
              <div class="pj-body">
                <p>A game controller you use with your body. It reads pose and hand landmarks from a webcam and turns gestures such as joining hands, jumping and crouching into game input.</p>
                <ul class="tags"><li>OpenCV</li><li>MediaPipe</li><li>NumPy</li><li>Pandas</li><li>PyAutoGUI</li></ul>
                <a class="link" href="https://github.com/s-u-s-h-ii/Reality-Gaming" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pj-shade"></div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pj" style="--i:1">
          <div class="pj-in">
            <div class="pj-viz">
              <canvas class="pj-art" data-art="ridges" role="img" aria-label="Animated ridgelines rising and falling like a signal"></canvas>
            </div>
            <div class="pj-info">
              <span class="pj-kind">Deep learning</span>
              <h3 class="pj-title" data-reveal>Muted Video to Text</h3>
              <div class="pj-body">
                <p>A lip-reading model that predicts text from silent video frames. 3D convolutions pick up spatial features, LSTMs follow the timing, and CTC loss aligns frames to characters. A Streamlit app wraps it.</p>
                <ul class="tags"><li>TensorFlow</li><li>Keras</li><li>OpenCV</li><li>Streamlit</li></ul>
                <a class="link" href="https://github.com/s-u-s-h-ii/Muted-Video-to-Text-Converter" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pj-shade"></div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pj" style="--i:2">
          <div class="pj-in">
            <div class="pj-viz">
              <canvas class="pj-art" data-art="pixels" role="img" aria-label="Animated pixel blobs that merge and split"></canvas>
            </div>
            <div class="pj-info">
              <span class="pj-kind">Generative media</span>
              <h3 class="pj-title" data-reveal>Text to Video</h3>
              <div class="pj-body">
                <p>Give it a prompt and it builds a short film. For each sentence it generates an image with a diffusion model and narrates it with text-to-speech. Each pair becomes a clip, and the clips join into one video.</p>
                <ul class="tags"><li>Diffusion pipeline</li><li>Google Text-to-Speech</li><li>MoviePy</li></ul>
                <a class="link" href="https://github.com/s-u-s-h-ii/Text-to-Video" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pj-shade"></div>
          </div>
        </article>

